# The instruction texts under src/prompt are embedded into the binary exactly as
# the checkout wrote them (`rust_embed`), and the pipeline splits several of them
# on a `---` line so each parallel agent gets its own variant. A checkout that
# rewrites line endings — Windows, where `core.autocrlf` is on by default — would
# ship bytes the repository does not hold and collapse those variants into one.
# LF is therefore pinned for this folder alone, in the store and on checkout; no
# other file in the repository is affected, raw-byte files included.
/src/prompt/** text eol=lf
